    "content": "Mogadishu, August 7, 2026 – Somali President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud met with General Sam Okiding, Deputy Chief of the Ugandan Defence Forces, at the presidential palace in Mogadishu on Friday. The meeting was part of the president's ongoing consultations with senior military officials who have gathered in the capital for a commanders' conference involving countries contributing troops to peacekeeping and anti-militant operations in Somalia.\n\nDuring the talks, the two officials discussed strengthening bilateral security cooperation, accelerating joint operations against extremist groups, and enhancing coordination among forces operating in Somalia. The summit aims to align strategies and improve effectiveness in stabilizing regions currently affected by insurgency.\n\nUganda has been a major contributor to the African Union Transition Mission in Somalia (ATMIS), formerly AMISOM, with thousands of troops deployed in several sectors. General Okiding's visit underscores the continued partnership between the two nations in addressing shared security challenges.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this meeting reflects ongoing international efforts to improve security, which is essential for development and the eventual return of displaced families. Stability in Somalia directly influences remittance flows and the safety of relatives and investments back home, making such high-level engagements of direct relevance to the diaspora community.\n\nThe conference, which began earlier this week, is expected to produce a joint action plan for the next phase of counterterrorism operations. President Mohamud has made security sector reform and dialogue with partner nations a priority of his administration.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/08/07/madaxweynaha-soomaaliya-oo-qaabilay-taliye-ku-xigeenka-ciidanka-difaaca-yugaandha/",
